{{Quote|We'll be sent to the spice mines of Kessel, smashed into who-knows-what!|C-3PO|<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
The '''spice mines of Kessel''', known as '''the Dark''' to veteran [[miner]]s,<ref name="TFV">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story: Tales from Vandor]]''</ref> were a series of [[labor camp]]s on the [[planet]] [[Kessel]], where [[Slavery|slaves]] from various [[species]], [[Wookiee]]s among them, were forced to [[Mining|mine]] a medicinal [[spice]] mineral into a dangerous drug. Spice mining was extremely dangerous, and slaves were thus used as [[Death|expendable]] labor. Life expectancy for [[humanoid]] species was two to three years,<ref name="heir">''[[Heir to the Jedi]]''</ref> while Wookiees had an expected survival time of three months.<ref name="rebelsvisual" /><ref name="Star Wars Rebels: Spark of Rebellion">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Spark of Rebellion]]''</ref> The [[Yaruba Family of Kessel]] turned a blind eye to the harvesting of spice on their world, living in luxurious sanctuaries in the southern hemisphere of the planet, while the spice mining took place in the northern hemisphere.

Spice mining was accomplished via the use of deep pits, mine shafts, and massive refineries.<ref name="rebelsvisual" />

Slaves in the mines used [[Bore-Driller]]s<ref name="G&G Bore-Drill">{{SWCT|set=Solo: A Star Wars Story - Gear & Gadgets|cardname=Kessel Spice Mine Portable Bore-Driller}}</ref> and [[vibropick]]s.<ref name="G&G Vibropick">{{SWCT|set=Solo: A Star Wars Story - Gear & Gadgets|cardname=Kessel Spice Mine Vibropick}}</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|It's a death sentence.|[[Hera Syndulla]]|<ref name="rebelsvisual" />}}
[[File:KesselSpiceMines-CGSWG.png|thumb|250px|right|The interior of the spice mines]]
The spice mines of Kessel were infamous for centuries.<ref name="Galactic Explorer's Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]''</ref> Approximately 10 [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Battle of Yavin]], the Empire sent [[Nakari Kelen]]'s [[Nakari Kelen's mother|mother]] to the spice mines of Kessel for writing the [[Music|song]] "[[Vader's Many Prosthetic Parts]]," along with the entire membership of the [[band]] [[Hakko Drazlip and the Tootle Froots]] for performing it.<ref name="heir" />

In [[10 BBY]],<ref name="Date Note">The timeline provided in ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]'' places [[Han Solo]]'s [[Kessel Run]] nine [[Standard year|years]] after the events of [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']]. As that film takes place in [[19 BBY]], we can deduce that the mission to [[Kessel]] and the subsequent Kessel Run took place in [[10 BBY]].</ref> [[Qi'ra]], [[Tobias Beckett]], and his [[Beckett's gang|crew]] (including [[Han Solo]] and [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]]) conducted a [[Raid on Kessel|raid]] on the mines in order to steal unrefined [[coaxium]] in order to pay off [[Crimson Dawn]] leader [[Dryden Vos]]. During the raid, workers (both organic slaves and droids) rose up against their [[Pyke Syndicate]] masters at the encouragement of [[L3-37]], leading to general chaos as the heist was performed. In the raid, [[Quay Tolsite]], [[Pyke]] [[Capo]] of the mines, was [[Death|killed]].<ref name="Solo:ASWS">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

Approximately fourteen years after the [[Galactic Republic]] was transformed into the [[Galactic Empire]], a group of Wookiees, including [[Wullffwarro]] and his son [[Kitwarr]], were sent to [[spice mine K76]] by [[Agent]] [[Alexsandr Kallus|Kallus]]. However, after a brief fracas involving a group of [[Spectres|rebels]] from [[Lothal]], the Wookiee slaves were rescued and brought aboard the heavily modified [[VCX-100 light freighter]] ''[[Ghost]]''.<ref name="rebelsvisual" />

When Imperial forces boarded the ''[[Tantive IV]]'', [[C-3PO]] was worried that he and [[R2-D2]] would probably be sent to the mines.<ref name="Episode IV" />

The spice mines of Kessel were mentioned in the ''[[Galactic Explorer's Guide]]'', a survival guide written by [[Hondo Ohnaka]] and [[DK-RA-43]].<ref name="Galactic Explorer's Guide" />

==Behind the scenes==
The spice mines of Kessel were first mentioned in the [[Star Wars: A New Hope (novelization)|novelization]] of the [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|original ''Star Wars'' film]] and also in the film itself. It later appeared in [[canon]] in ''[[Star Wars Rebels: Spark of Rebellion]]''.

For the [[2018]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|''Star Wars'' Anthology]] film ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'', the open-cast [[copper]] mines of [[Wikipedia:Spain|Spain]] and the sulfuric hot springs of the [[Wikipedia:Dallol (volcano)|Dallol volcano]] in [[Wikipedia:Ethiopia|Ethiopia]] influenced the look of the spice mines of Kessel and were considered too as shooting locations. In addition, the Kessel mines control room was inspired by the mid-century control rooms in the [[Wikipedia:Soviet Union|Soviet Union]], it draws more specifically from the control room of the [[Wikipedia:Fawley Power Station|Fawley Power Station]] in [[Wikipedia:Hampshire|Hampshire]], [[Wikipedia:England|England]].<ref name="Art of Solo">''[[The Art of Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

An idea proposed for ''Solo'' but not used in the finished version of the film was to have a [[Wookiee]] slave gang working at the mines and being supervised by [[stormtrooper]]s. This idea was ultimately dropped as the film shows Quay Tolsite and [[S1D6-SA-5]] as the supervisors of the mines.<ref name="Art of Solo" />

